  "body": "What happens: a Drill operation added with its default source (`stock`), then `detect_holes`, answers \"no drilled holes found in the source model\". The source is the stock, not the model, so the message points the wrong way. In the local-model MCP benchmark of 2026-11-22, several models gave up at this step.\n\nExpected: the refusal says the operation's source is the stock and suggests `source: <model name>`, naming the document's models.\n\nDone means: the message names the actual source and the fix; a test pins the wording.\n",
